course: dictionary
lesson: 13245
title: The geranium: a plant in your garden
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A geranium is a garden or pot plant with bright red, pink, white or purple flowers. You often see them on window sills and balconies. «Mum put a pot of red geraniums on the window sill.» Here, the pot is the container and the geraniums are the plants growing in it.
explain: The word can also mean a wild plant of the same family, which is sometimes called cranesbill. Look at the clue: a wild plant grows outside without anyone planting it. «The wild geraniums along the path had purple flowers.» So the word can mean a garden plant or a wild one.
explain: Scientists and gardeners study geraniums to learn how plants grow. Their leaves are often round and furry. «We took geranium cuttings from Grandma's garden.» A cutting is a small piece of plant that can grow into a new plant.
fact: A geranium is a garden or pot plant with bright red, pink, white or purple flowers.
fact: The leaves of a geranium are often round and furry.
fact: A wild geranium is also called cranesbill.
fact: A cutting is a small piece of plant that can grow into a new plant.
fact: The plural of geranium is geraniums.
exercise: «Mum put a pot of red geraniums on the window sill.» What is a geranium? | A kind of window | A tall tree with no flowers | A type of bird | *A garden or pot plant with bright flowers
exercise: Which of these is another name for a wild geranium? | Daisy | Dandelion | *Cranesbill | Bluebell
exercise: «We took geranium cuttings from Grandma's garden.» What is a cutting? | *A small piece of plant that can grow into a new one | A pair of scissors | A bunch of flowers picked for a vase | A sharp tool for cutting grass
test: What is the plural of geranium? | geraniumes | geraniuma | geranium's | *geraniums
test: Which part of a geranium is often round and furry? | *Its leaves | Its roots | Its pot | Its flowers
exam: Which of these is true about geraniums? | They have no leaves | They are animals | They only grow in deserts | *They can be pot plants with bright red, pink, white or purple flowers
